When getOverrideLocaleConfig is called for a package that is not installed
for the target user, it previously threw an IllegalArgumentException because
isPackageOwnedByCaller checked the package UID and threw if it was < 0.

This caused crashes in Settings (which calls getOverrideLocaleConfig via
LocaleConfig constructor to check if apps support locales) when it queried
packages that were not installed in the current user profile (e.g. test packages
only installed in user 0 but queried in user 10).

This change adds a package existence check at the beginning of
getOverrideLocaleConfig, returning null immediately if the package is not found,
restoring the previous behavior and preventing crashes.

Bug: 495409704
Bug: 529474515
Test: atest FrameworksServicesTests:LocaleManagerServiceTest
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Change-Id: I12dea12f5dc790edb45091bc3eaca59748f3b273

(cherry picked from commit 3ee6771f2a38de2a4386b0981a522383a645c093)
